@normanmaurer The javadocs for `ByteBuf#getBytes` state that the `fileChannel` position is not being modified. Does this not imply that all calls to this method start writing from the beginning of the file (and thus overwrite each other)?

`written` is now also effectively unused; shouldn't this line be `written = buffer.getBytes(...);`?.

see https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/10425.
